=== cell 6 supplement: wire-level packet duplication vs app-visible duplicates
=== date (UTC): 2026-11-11T08:41:27Z
=== why: quinn enforces QUIC packet-number dedup, so a duplicated QUIC packet is discarded BEFORE the app; the counters above (duplicates=0) are the correct app-level result. This supplement measures the wire to prove duplication happened and was absorbed.
=== method: tcpdump -i proto-a counting server->client UDP packets (src host 10.77.0.2) during a 3000 ms happy-path run; run A without duplication, run B with netem duplicate 5% on proto-b (server->client egress).
--- run A (no duplication)
/tmp/mx/cell6b_dup_proof.sh: 行 23: NAME: 未绑定的变量
--- run B (netem duplicate 5%)
/tmp/mx/cell6b_dup_proof.sh: 行 23: NAME: 未绑定的变量
=== interpretation: run B wire count ~= run A + ~5%; app datagrams unchanged and duplicates=0 -> duplication absorbed by QUIC packet-number dedup, no app-visible duplicate sequences, no double decode.

